name issue_331_low_bandwidth_av_offset_seed4
describe low_bandwidth with seed 4: lip sync raises the audio delay past 2 s and the audio buffer must hold it (issue #331)
# NetEq's PacketBuffer holds NetEq::Config::max_packets_in_buffer = 200 packets and flushes all of them only when
# full (packet_buffer.cc InsertPacket); DelayConstraints caps the minimum delay at 75 % of that buffer (3 s of 20 ms
# audio). Ours flushed above 100 packets (2 s), so once RtpStreamsSynchronizer had raised the audio delay past 2 s the
# flush threw it away and the A/V offset came back (issue #331).
# Seed 4: sync.av_offset_p95_ms 2355 -> 1892 ms (libwebrtc 1900 on main's compare-webrtc), median 1271 -> 1065 ms.
# low_bandwidth seeds 1-10 mean 1765 -> 1708 ms (libwebrtc 1576, band 188); seeds 1-40 mean 1839 -> 1694 ms.
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=150kbps delay=40ms queue=500ms
seed 4
# Guard rail moved by #356 (program.md 0.2). Provisional lock, accepted by the Owner on 2026-10-24 and tracked to #356, now #360 (below): with the receiver's RTT measured over XR
# RRTR/DLRR as libwebrtc's, seed 4 reads p95 1937 ms and p50 1163 ms (#350 had `< 1900` and `< 1150`, ours 1892 and
# 1065 then). libwebrtc seed 4: p95 1900. low_bandwidth seeds 1-10 p95 mean: libwebrtc 1576 (band 188), main 1708,
# with XR 1724; p50 mean: libwebrtc 931, main 951, with XR 978.
# Issue #355 (rate_utilization_tracker on by default, as libwebrtc): with the tracker and XR together, seed 4 reads p95
# 1880 ms and p50 1112 ms, so the lines go back to #350's bounds (libwebrtc seed 4: p95 1900).
# #356 closed with nothing left to port after #367 (main 74e965c, seeds 1-10: no gap on issue_346_reconfigure_capacity_drop).
# #360 (PR #378, RTCP first-report timing) on top of #324 (quality scaling on): seed 4 reads p95 1181 ms and p50 846 ms
# (main bbee233: 1283 and 937), well inside both bounds, so this is a plain lock again and no longer tracked to an issue.
# Merged with #345 (SPS VUI rewrite; main fbf2f32 reads 1926/1162 under its provisional < 1950 / < 1175): seed 4 reads
# p95 874 ms and p50 466 ms with #360's RTCP timing, so the tighter lock stays.
expect sync.av_offset_p95_ms < 1900
expect sync.av_offset_p50_ms < 1150
expect audio.concealed_pct < 5
